Z||000005||Jay||11-17-2001||06:18 PM||||If you are going to go through with the trouble of using an Import engine why not use the tranny that was ment for it?  You have to custom make the mounts anyway, so why not do it for the trany also? That way you don't have to mess around too much with the ecm. The ecm doesn't know it's in a domestic car.  Then you get custom 1/2 shafts made or convert to the Imports shafts,hubs,spindles, brakes ect.  That's what I did with the Northstar.  There are more performance parts for the Imports than for our cars, like brakes, lowering kits ect.  <P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig2_copy_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Sootah||11-17-2001||08:07 PM||||Well I was just wondering if there were any imports that used the same patterns as our domestics. (Mounting points, tranny mating, etc) Isuzu made the tranny for some of our cars, so the bellhousing I figured may mate up. By the same logic I figured that some may use GM's 60º V6 block mounting points.||||reg||1
