Z||000018||Return of Fiero||11-20-2001||09:55 AM||||Just curious, why does the 3.5 keep getting brought up with the olds? the olds used the 3.4 or the 3800 from what i remeber. also the 3.1, and every other chevy engine. the 3.5 if what is used in the dodge. i have 2 taxis that are intrepids that are 3.5, and one that is a 3.0. i have had ford that were 3.0 and the 302. i have had GM that have been (luminas and caprices) 3100, 3400, 3800, 305 and 350's but never a GM with a 3.5. oh, by the way, the Fords are bad for cabs, they break down 2-3 times as much as the GM. back to my point, what olds (you know, GM oldsmobile) has a 3.5, as no cutlass, or other GM i have had for a taxi has had a 3.5. just curiousity running rampid here.<BR>Myke<BR>||||reg||1
